{"availability":"available","full":"TheMEGALODON55681/Neurolens","name":"Neurolens","description":"EfficientNet-B3 brain MRI classifier with patient-level splitting (zero data leakage), test-time augmentation, and Grad-CAM attention maps. Trained on 4,564 images across 4 tumor types — 96.51% accuracy on truly unseen patients.","category":"Education","language":"Jupyter Notebook","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-27T07:31:38Z","updated":"2026-08-29T16:04:25Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/TheMEGALODON55681/NeuroLens","topics":["brain-tumor-classification","computer-vision","deep-learning","efficientnet","explainable-ai","gradcam","gradio","healthcare-ai","huggingface-spaces","image-classification","medical-imaging","mri-classification","neural-network","pytorch","transfer-learning"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/TheMEGALODON55681/NeuroLens","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:55.144Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:55.144Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:55.144Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T22:34:55.144Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An honest brain MRI tumor classifier — built to expose the data leakage hiding in most public implementations.","Figshare provides three tumor types with patient IDs — the essential ingredient for patient-level splitting. Br35H provides healthy controls (no-tumor images) that Figshare doesn't include. Most aggregated datasets that combine these sources strip the patient IDs in the process, which silently makes proper splitting impossible. Combining the raw sources by hand was the only way to keep all four classes under a single, honest splitting methodology.","A documented asymmetry: Br35H does not provide patient IDs, so each Br35H image is treated as an independent pseudo-patient. The no-tumor split is therefore effectively image-level while the three tumor splits are patient-level. This asymmetry is disclosed openly rather than buried — it would be fully resolved only by access to a dataset with patient-level healthy controls."],"features":["Understand architecture instantly — no need to read all files","Spot design flaws — identifies isolated components, weak cohesion areas","Find integration points — shows which nodes bridge communities (high-impact when changed)","Plan refactors — community cohesion scores suggest where to split modules"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/TheMEGALODON55681/Neurolens/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a589a4b6c030d3219c47d01e60a01b5a4ab9f4baf0be16ff23c146cc4fc6ea64","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:55.255Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:55.255Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An honest brain MRI tumor classifier — built to expose the data leakage hiding in most public implementations.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/TheMEGALODON55681/Neurolens/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"a589a4b6c030d3219c47d01e60a01b5a4ab9f4baf0be16ff23c146cc4fc6ea64","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/TheMEGALODON55681/Neurolens/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:55.255Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-29T16:04:25Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/TheMEGALODON55681/Neurolens/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:55.256Z","hash":"a589a4b6c030d3219c47d01e60a01b5a4ab9f4baf0be16ff23c146cc4fc6ea64","originalBytes":23727,"storedBytes":23727,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["tumor","model","class","meningioma","test","patient","brain","mri","accuracy","training","dataset","architecture","grad-cam","image","split","errors","figshare","glioma","images","no-tumor","patients","br35h","graph","most","patient-level","slices","attention","confidence","data","different","neurolens","pituitary","splitting","demo","docs","each","full","head","number","only","prediction","project","rather","set","these","v